[Music]  biodiversity you've probably heard the  word but what does it mean and why  should we care  biodiversity is the variety of life on  Earth that supports the health of our  planet which helps us in many ways  biodiversity is at the heart of nature  cleaning the water we drink purify the  air we breathe keeping our soils fertile  and providing us with medicine  nature regulates the climate and it does  all this and more for free we need to  look after nature if we want it to look  after us but all around the world  animals plants and the space they need  to live in are disappearing in the EU  42% of mammals 15% of birds and 45% of  butterflies and reptiles are under  threat as landscapes once rich in  biodiversity become ever more scarce  invasive species are upsetting the  balance of nature causing 12 billion  euros damage every year but the good  news is biodiversity loss can be stopped  it's time to invest in protecting and  restoring our life-support systems we  need to leave space for nature for its  sake and for ours find out more online  about the EU efforts to halt  biodiversity loss its network of  protected natural areas Natura 2000 and  how you can get involved  you  [Music]

